  "scope_id": "PC-SIZE-GRID-20261020-001",
  "title": "Polynomial calculus size of Tseitin formulas on grids is exponential in the side",
  "subject": "Size lower bounds for algebraic refutations of Tseitin formulas on bounded-degree planar graphs",
  "conclusion": "Over any field of characteristic other than 2, every polynomial calculus refutation (0/1 basis, with or without twin variables) of the Tseitin formula of the a x b grid has size 2^Omega(min(a,b)), and size 2^O(min(a,b)) poly(ab) suffices. Since PCR simulates resolution, resolution needs 2^Omega(min(a,b)) on grids as well.",
